menu "MQTT Configuration"

    config MQTT_TOPIC_PREFIX
        string "MQTT topic prefix"

    config MQTT_MAX_INFLIGHT_QOS
        int "Maximum in-flight QoS>0 messages"
        default 16
        range 1 100
        help
            Upper bound on the number of unacknowledged QoS 1/2 PUBLISH packets
            allowed in flight at once. Must stay below the broker's MQTT5 Receive
            Maximum (commonly 20) or the broker rejects publishes with "Client send
            more than N QoS1 and QoS2 PUBLISH packet without no ack". Publishing
            applies back-pressure: a producer task blocks until an in-flight slot
            frees (an ACK arrives) or the connection drops.

    config MQTT_INFLIGHT_TTL_MS
        int "In-flight QoS message TTL (ms)"
        default 5000
        range 100 60000
        help
            Maximum time an in-flight QoS>0 publish is allowed to occupy a slot
            without being acknowledged (MQTT_EVENT_PUBLISHED) or reported deleted
            (MQTT_EVENT_DELETED). Once this elapses the slot is reclaimed anyway.
            This is a self-healing backstop: esp-mqtt can silently drop a message
            from its outbox without any event, which would otherwise leak the slot
            permanently until the next disconnect. Keep it above the broker's
            typical round-trip ACK latency but low enough that a lost message
            doesn't stall publishing for long.


endmenu
